<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at -1.17 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at -1.17 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4385 to the dollar, up from 3.4565 on Tuesday and at 1.8790 to the mark, up from 1.9045, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.17 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesday's fix at -2.03 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
